From: EngineOS maintainers
Subject: Do not emit terminal alerts to headless graphical clients

EngineOS graphical clients participate in tmux session, focus, input, status,
and sizing state, but do not open a terminal and therefore have no tty term
capability table.  The ordinary alert path must not call tty_putcode() or
status_message_set() for these clients.  Graphical status and notifications
are exported through the frontend model instead.

diff --git a/alerts.c b/alerts.c
index 25f6a445..f0f74a11 100644
--- a/alerts.c
+++ b/alerts.c
@@ -310 +310,2 @@ alerts_set_message(struct winlink *wl, const char *type, const char *option)
-		if (c->session != wl->session || c->flags & CLIENT_CONTROL)
+		if (c->session != wl->session ||
+		    c->flags & (CLIENT_CONTROL|CLIENT_GRAPHICAL))
